From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:53:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 103/103] fix(warrants): stamp gc.kind=workflow so filed
 warrants actually pour (gcp-w310)

Pool demand detection polls for a ready, unassigned bead carrying BOTH
gc.kind=workflow and gc.routed_to -- that pair is what makes a bead a
pollable workflow root. Every warrant-filing template in the pack stamped
only gc.routed_to, so a filed warrant was a plain bead wearing a routing
label: no demand was ever signalled, no dog was ever spawned, and the
warrant sat open and unassigned forever while every status surface stayed
green. gascity-9qfg sat routed to the dog pool with zero dog sessions ever
appearing in `gc session list`; per the mayor's note two earlier batches
went unclaimed for two days the same way.

The bead named four sites (three in mol-deacon-patrol, one in
mol-witness-patrol). Two more carry the identical defect and are fixed
here too, because leaving them would have left the bug live:

- gastown/agents/boot/prompt.template.md -- boot has no formula, so its
  warrant command is authoritative rather than a copy (gastown/README.md
  documents this as one of the three restatement exceptions). Every
  warrant boot files for a stuck deacon would still have been inert.
- gastown/formulas/mol-shutdown-dance.toml -- the preamble is the canonical
  recipe every warrant producer is written from, so leaving it would have
  taught the broken shape to the next one.

The fix is the metadata key alone. It is deliberately NOT the "pour via
sling/mol" alternative the bead offers as a second option: mol-shutdown-
dance states its own dispatch contract as "this formula is not poured with
template vars -- dispatch is a claimed task bead", and the dog prompt reads
target/reason/requester off $GC_BEAD_ID with no separate warrant_id. Slinging
would have required redesigning that whole path; marking the warrant as its
own workflow root leaves the dog's claim contract untouched.

Guarded by a new detector in the drift test, alongside the pool-return and
warrant-dedup invariants it already enforces -- same silent-orphan class,
where the bead looks healthy by inspection and nothing errors. The detector
is scoped to warrant creation rather than every routed create: the routing
key alone is correct on a bead a claimed session picks up by assignment,
and only a pool-dispatched create needs the root marker.

Validation: the new detector was run against the pre-fix text of all four
patched files via `git show HEAD:<path>` and flagged exactly the six sites
above (red), then `pytest tests/test_prompt_formula_command_drift.py` at
9 passed (green). Full sweep: go vet clean, golangci-lint 0 issues,
validate_registry.py ok, go test ./... ok.

Pre-existing and NOT from this branch: tests/test_no_bare_bd_commands.py
fails on base 8daf4447 over prose in docs/design/reaper-budget-starvation.md,
reproduced from a pristine detached worktree. Filed as gcp-98gh (P1,
discovered-from gcp-w310) and notified to the witness. It reddens GitHub CI
on integration and therefore on this PR, while all four configured rig gates
stay green -- that gate gap is the more consequential half of gcp-98gh.

